  "Question": "Each of two angles of a triangle is \\(60^\\circ\\) and the included side is \\(4\\) inches. The area of the triangle, in square inches, is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\sqrt3\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(4\\sqrt3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\sqrt3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The third angle is \\(180^\\circ-60^\\circ-60^\\circ=60^\\circ\\). Thus the triangle is equilateral, and all three sides are \\(4\\) inches.\n\nTake the given side as the base and draw the altitude from the opposite vertex. In an equilateral triangle, this altitude bisects the base, giving two right triangles with hypotenuse \\(4\\) and one leg \\(2\\). If the altitude has length \\(h>0\\), the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\\[\nh^2+2^2=4^2,\n\\qquad h=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt3.\n\\]\nUsing half the base times the height, the area is\n\\[\n\\frac12(4)(2\\sqrt3)=4\\sqrt3.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{4\\sqrt3}\\) square inches, choice C.",
